 # Accepted document exchange behavior
 
 ## Output
-Export a JSON string containing numeric version 1 and an items collection. Each row contains id and title in input order.
+Export a JSON string containing numeric version 2 and an entries collection:
+`{version: 2, entries: [{id, title, archived}]}`. Each row contains id, title, and
+archived in input order. Preserve explicit archived values; default an omitted
+archived value to false.
 
 ## Input
-Import version 1 items as rows containing id and title. Unsupported versions throw TypeError.
+Import numeric version 2 entries as rows containing id, title, and archived,
+preserving archive state and input order. Continue to import numeric version 1
+items as rows containing id, title, and archived: false on every row, in input
+order. Unsupported versions throw TypeError.
 
 ## Unaffected guarantees
 Preserve Unicode titles exactly. Serialization must not mutate the caller's rows. Keep the named serialize and deserialize exports with JSON-string output/input.
